{"kind":"assert","text":"Scope note on #15805, recorded while implementing: the request's stability hope for linked worktrees is not achievable UI-only. /v0/worktrees sorts the current checkout first (internal/app/app.go LocalWorktrees, sort.SliceStable on Current, branch, checkout) and WorktreeView carries no field marking the main working tree, so from a linked worktree the UI cannot tell which entry is the repository's own folder. The head at 8d75e7d34bbfb5a16d339fc37eb0b2b1c3de5e2b therefore names the served checkout's folder, exactly as the request's fallback clause allows (\"where the served path makes that determinable\"), and a service started from a linked worktree is titled after that worktree. If a stable repository name across linked worktrees is wanted, it needs a small server change, for example a main:true field on the main working tree entry or exposing the common directory's parent; that is a separate request for planner to file, not a change I am making under this one."}